/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:65:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:66:Sort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:67:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:68:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:69:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:70:- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:71:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:72:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:73:- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:74:- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:75:- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:76:- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:77:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:78:Key insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:79:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:80:</reference_puzzle>
