/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:83:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:84:Fill rectangular cavities in a template shape by placing source sprites into matching holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:85:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:86:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:87:- bg = most common color. A dominant "base" color forms a large frame/template with rectangular gaps.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:88:- Small colored sprites sit outside the template region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:89:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:90:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:91:- The base color (largest connected component excluding bg) defines the template bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:92:- Each rectangular hole inside the template matches exactly one outside sprite by size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:93:- Place each sprite into its matching cavity; output is the filled template bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:94:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:95:Key insight: Sprite bounding boxes match cavity dimensions exactly — it's a jigsaw-fit puzzle where each piece has a unique slot.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:96:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:97:</reference_puzzle>
