/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:117:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:118:Simulate particles along a path with alternating turn direction at collisions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:119:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:120:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:121:- Top-left: 2x2 monochrome blocks define a repeating color cycle (left-to-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:122:- Isolated single pixels of a cycle color: start markers adjacent to the path.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:123:- A 2x2 monochrome block of a distinct color: end marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:124:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:125:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:126:- Each start marker launches a particle moving straight, painting cycle colors in order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:127:- On hitting a boundary, paint that cell with the end color and turn 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:128:- Turn direction alternates: odd collisions → left (CCW), even → right (CW).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:129:- If the scheduled turn is blocked, the particle stops.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:130:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:131:Key insight: The alternating left/right turn rule is the core mechanism; without it the path would be trivial.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:132:</description>
