/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:171:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:172:Eject content pixels from cup-shaped frames outward along each cup's tail direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:173:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:174:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:175:- bg = background. Hollow cup/Y/funnel frames, each a unique border color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:176:- Each cup has a convergent tail spike on one side and an open mouth on the opposite side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:177:- Content pixels (a single non-border color per cup) sit inside the cup's mouth interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:178:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:179:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:180:- For each cup, identify its tail spike and tail direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:181:- Erase all content pixels from the mouth interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:182:- Draw a straight line of content-colored pixels from the spike outward in the tail direction,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:183:  one pixel per erased content pixel; cells beyond the grid edge are dropped.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:184:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:185:Key insight: The tail spike is the unique convergent point whose outward direction is opposite
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:186:the mouth opening where the content lives.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:187:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:188:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:189:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:190:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="e87109e9" lines="68-83">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:191:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:192:Emit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:193:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:194:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:195:- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:196:- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:197:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:198:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:199:- Remove the legend from the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:200:- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:201:- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:202:- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:203:- Beams stop at grid edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:204:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:205:Key insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:206:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:207:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:208:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:209:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="b99e7126" lines="34-48">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:210:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:211:Scale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:212:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:213:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:214:- Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:215:- Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:217:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:218:- Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:219:- Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:220:- Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:221:- Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:222:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:223:Key insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:224:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:225:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:226:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:227:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="8698868d" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:228:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:229:Match sprites to frames by connected-hole count, then nest each sprite inside its frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:231:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:232:- bg = azure (8). Large hollow squares (frames) arranged in a grid; smaller filled squares (sprites) placed elsewhere.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:233:- Each frame and sprite has a distinct color. Sprites may contain holes (non-sprite-color pixels).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:235:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:236:- Frames form a regular grid; some may be bg-colored (invisible).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:237:- Count connected hole regions inside each frame's interior and each sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:238:- Pair each frame with the sprite sharing the same hole count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:239:- Place the matched sprite inside the frame border; recolor sprite holes to the frame's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:241:Key insight: The matching key is the number of connected hole components, not hole area or color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:242:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:243:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:244:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:245:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="1ae2feb7" lines="30-45">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:246:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:247:Extend row bars periodically across the opposite side of a separator column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:248:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:249:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:250:- bg = background. A near-solid vertical separator divides the grid into two sides.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:251:- One side contains horizontal colored bars; the other side is blank target space.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:252:- Bars may be stacked by row and may sit at different distances from the separator.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:253:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:254:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:255:- Identify the separator as the column whose non-bg cells are one color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:256:- Treat the denser side as the bar side and collect each contiguous row run.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:257:- Process bars from nearest to farthest from the separator; for each bar, paint its
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:258:  color every bar-length cells into the blank side without overwriting earlier paint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:259:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:260:Key insight: Each bar's length is the period for its extension, and nearer bars claim target cells first.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:261:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:262:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:263:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:264:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="b10624e5" lines="24-39">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:265:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:266:Replicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:267:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:268:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:269:- Grid divided into four quadrants by a full-row and full-column divider of a single non-bg color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:270:- Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:271:- The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:272:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:273:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:274:- Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:275:- For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:276:- Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:277:- Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:278:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:279:Key insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:280:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:281:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:282:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:283:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="78332cb0" lines="10-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:284:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:285:Reorder 5×5 blocks into a connected strip by matching edge foreground pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:286:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:287:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:288:- bg = background; sep = divider color (full row/column lines).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:289:- Several 5×5 sprite blocks in a grid, separated by sep lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:290:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:291:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:292:- Two blocks "connect" when their facing edges share foreground pixels at the same offset (e.g., A's right edge ∩ B's left edge).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:293:- Chain all blocks in the orientation (horizontal or vertical) that admits a complete sequence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:294:- Output is a 1×N strip of blocks in chain order, separated by sep lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:295:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:296:Key insight: Edge-contact overlap determines both block ordering and output orientation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:297:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:298:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:299:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:300:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="da515329" lines="11-24">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:301:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:302:Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:303:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:304:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:305:- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:306:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:307:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:308:- Each arm tip launches a "turtle" heading 90° right of its outward direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:309:- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:310:- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:311:- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:312:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:313:Key insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:314:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:315:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:316:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:317:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="136b0064" lines="25-39">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:318:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:319:Draw a polyline by decoding 3x3 glyph instructions read across a divided grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:320:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:321:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:322:- Left of a full-height vertical divider: 3x3 colored glyphs on bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:323:- Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:324:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:325:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:326:- Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:327:- Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:328:- Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:329:- Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:330:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:331:Key insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:332:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:333:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:334:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:335:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="eval" puzzle_id="eee78d87" lines="40-55">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:336:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:337:Decode the colored 3x3 contour motif into a 16x16 periodic lattice with the motif stamped in maroon at the center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:338:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:339:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:340:- The grid is 6x6 with orange background and one non-orange color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:341:- The non-orange pixels have a tight 3x3 bbox containing one contour glyph.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:342:- The glyph is one of the task's period-3 contour forms: plus, H, X, or four corners.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:343:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:344:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:345:- Decode the 3x3 glyph into the period-3 orange phase tile.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:346:- Fill a black 16x16 canvas by repeating that orange phase tile.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:347:- Tile the original 3x3 glyph 2x2 and recolor its true pixels to maroon in the centered 6x6 region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:348:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:349:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:350:- The colored object is not copied at its input location; it is a small contour code whose phase tells where orange appears in the repeated lattice.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:351:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:352:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:353:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:354:<reference_puzzle index="20" source="eval" puzzle_id="20270e3b" lines="7-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:355:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:356:Connect two sprites using matching connector pixels, then tight-crop.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:357:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:358:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:359:- Background color `bg`, sprite color `obj`, connector color `ctrl` (small, 2 components).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:360:- Two main foreground sprites, plus possibly tiny detached pixels belonging to one sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:361:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:362:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:363:- Identify the **base** sprite (closest to grid top-left).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:364:- Translate the other sprite so its connector sits one cell above the base's connector.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:365:- Stamp the plug onto the base; remove connectors (recolor `ctrl` to `obj`).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:366:- Output is the tight crop around all non-background pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:367:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:368:Key insight: The connector pixels define the unique docking point and direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:369:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:370:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:371:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:372:你的任务：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:373:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:374:创新方式包括但不限于：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:375:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:376:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed50410689/5/prompt.md:377:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程"。
